@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Customer Partner Account Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki partner account information transfers properly to customer.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate past static start and end dates
	* I generate future static start and end dates
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | cstm.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | cstm.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | CSTM                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | cstm.partner2                      |
	| Email Address | cstm.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | CSTM                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner2                           |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | CSTPARCSTPAR                  | |
	| Name   | Cstpar - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Cstpar - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "cstm.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Cstpar - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Member |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "cstm.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Cstpar - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Manager |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	* I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Cstpar - ${staticProjectName}" assigned to the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Cstpar - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| CSTM Partner1  |
	| CSTM Partner2  |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| CSTPARCSTPAR |
	| KORCSTKORCST |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Cstpar - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| CSTPARCSTPAR |
	| KORCSTKORCST |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| cstm.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| cstm.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| cstm.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| cstm.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| cstm.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| cstm.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| cstm.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| cstm.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| cstm.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	| cstm.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken   |

Scenario: View partner first line support and customer on Customer
	If a projects order becomes inactive in OSB, existing partner workers on that project should have their tags removed and also be removed from their organization in Zendesk.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | KORCSTKORCST                     | |
	| Language                   | English                          | |
	| Name                       | Korcst - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	And I assign the team with the name "Cstpar - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign the team with the name "Cstpar - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	And I log into the customer homepage as "${staticCustomerAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticCustomerAdminPassword}"